{
  "sn12.36:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.36 ",
  "sn12.36:0.2": "4. Kaḷāra the Aristocrat ",
  "sn12.36:0.3": "Ignorance is a Requirement (2nd) ",
  "sn12.36:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.36:1.2": "“Ignorance is a requirement for choices. ",
  "sn12.36:1.3": "Choices are a requirement for consciousness. … ",
  "sn12.36:1.4": "That is how this entire mass of suffering originates. ",
  "sn12.36:2.1": "Mendicants, you might say, ‘What are old age and death, and who do they belong to?’ Or you might say, ‘Old age and death are one thing, who they belong to is another.’ But both of these mean the same thing, only the phrasing differs. ",
  "sn12.36:2.2": "If you have the view that the soul and the body are one and the same, there is no living of the spiritual life. ",
  "sn12.36:2.3": "If you have the view that the soul is one thing, the body another, there is no living of the spiritual life. ",
  "sn12.36:2.4": "Avoiding these two extremes, the Realized One teaches by the middle way: ",
  "sn12.36:2.5": "‘Rebirth is a requirement for old age and death.’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.1": "‘What is rebirth …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.2": "‘What is continued existence …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.3": "‘What is grasping …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.4": "‘What is craving …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.5": "‘What is feeling …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.6": "‘What is contact …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.7": "‘What are the six sense fields …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.8": "‘What are name and form …’ ",
  "sn12.36:3.9": "‘What is conscio